---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Warranty terms" description="The one-year limited warranty on Ecozenin wall decor.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>One-year limited warranty</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated October 8, 2026</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        {site.legalName} warrants each product to the original buyer against defects in materials and workmanship
        for one year from the date of purchase.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>
        If a covered defect appears within the year, we repair the product, replace it, or refund the price you
        paid. We choose which, and we cover the shipping for a replacement.
      </p>

      <h2>What isn't covered</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Accidental damage, misuse or alteration.</li>
        <li>Damage from installing or hanging the product in a way the instructions don't describe.</li>
        <li>Normal wear, including gradual fading or colour change.</li>
        <li>Products bought from anyone other than Ecozenin's official Amazon store.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to claim</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> with a photo of the problem and proof
        of purchase, such as your Amazon order confirmation. <a href="/register">Registering your warranty</a> isn't
        required, but it speeds things up.
      </p>

      <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
      <p>
        This warranty gives you specific legal rights. You may have other rights that vary from state to state, and
        nothing here limits them. To the extent the law allows, {site.legalName} isn't liable for incidental or
        consequential damages; some states don't allow that limit, so it may not apply to you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
